inksight
========

This package wraps the model and example code published with "InkSight:
Offline-to-Online Handwriting Conversion by Teaching Vision-Language Models to
Read and Write" (Mitrevski, Rak, Schnitzler, Li, Maksai, Berent, Musat; TMLR 2025):

    https://github.com/google-research/inksight   (colab.ipynb)

The original notebook code is
    Copyright 2024 Google LLC
and is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (see LICENSE).

Changes: the notebook's pre- and post-processing were reorganised into a small
class hierarchy with pluggable runners and word detectors; the graph's
SentencePiece ops can be swapped for the sentencepiece Python package where
tensorflow-text is unavailable (Windows).

Model weights
-------------
The package bundles the released InkSight-Small-p checkpoint
(small-p-cpu, https://storage.googleapis.com/derendering_model/small-p-cpu.zip,
also https://huggingface.co/Derendering/InkSight-Small-p) in compressed form
under src/inksight/vendor/model, unmodified. The authors release the model,
the supplementary derendering dataset and the human-tracing data under
Apache-2.0 for RESEARCH, NON-COMMERCIAL use only, because they derive from
non-commercial research datasets. The model card also asks that it not be used
for privacy-intruding purposes such as forging handwriting. These terms apply
to the bundled weights and to ink produced with them.

This is not an officially supported Google product.
